<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Primary Dealers see 2.1 GDP growth in '97.</title>
<headline>Belgian Primary Dealers see 2.1 GDP growth in '97.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are forecasts published by the Belgian Primary Dealers Association (BPDA) in its latest newsletter:</p>
<p>					    1996 *    1997   1997</p>
<p>							  BPDA   EC/OECD</p>
<p> Real Gross Domestic Product	+1.4	+2.1   +2.2</p>
<p> Inflation (averages)		 n/a	 +2.1   +2.0</p>
<p> Current account (% of GDP) (1)   +5.2	+5.2   +5.6</p>
<p> Budget deficit (% of GDP)	  -3.4	-2.9   -2.9</p>
<p>NOTE - * Belgian central bank estimates; (1) for Belgo- Luxembourg economic union (Belgian transactions generated nearly 80 pct of the surplus in 1996).</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
